# Use VS Code REST Client or copy requests into Postman.
# Run requests individually. These demo requests create disposable visitor data.
@api = http://127.0.0.1:5000/api

### Health: must return 200
GET {{api}}/health

### Backend contract: money is integer minor units; writes need stable keys
GET {{api}}/openapi.json

### Independent retail visitor, with no owner credentials
# @name retail
POST {{api}}/demo/start
Content-Type: application/json

{"scenario":"retail"}

### Sample catalog and stock
GET {{api}}/demo/catalog
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}

### Create a cart
# @name cart
POST {{api}}/demo/checkouts
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}
Idempotency-Key: review-cart-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Server prices one sample item
# @name priced
PATCH {{api}}/demo/checkouts/{{cart.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}
Idempotency-Key: review-lines-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"revision":1,"lines":[{"item_id":{{retail.response.body.data.item_ids[0]}},"quantity":"1"}]}

### Cash payment (re-send the SAME request/key to check retry safety)
POST {{api}}/demo/checkouts/{{cart.response.body.data.id}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}
Idempotency-Key: review-cash-{{cart.response.body.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method":"cash","amount_minor":{{priced.response.body.data.total_minor}}}

### Complete once; duplicate request returns same invoice
# @name completed
POST {{api}}/demo/checkouts/{{cart.response.body.data.id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}
Idempotency-Key: review-complete-{{cart.response.body.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Receipt data and stock result
GET {{api}}/demo/receipts/{{completed.response.body.data.invoice_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}

###
GET {{api}}/demo/stock
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}

### Separate bakery visitor includes a sample cake booking and deposit
# @name bakery
POST {{api}}/demo/start
Content-Type: application/json

{"scenario":"bakery"}

###
GET {{api}}/demo/bakery-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{bakery.response.body.data.token}}

### Restart expires only this visitor's session; use returned new token afterward
POST {{api}}/demo/restart
Authorization: Bearer {{retail.response.body.data.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Protected business route must return 401 without an owner/staff JWT
GET {{api}}/counter/checkouts

# Business manual review: log in through POST /auth/login using your existing
# identifier/password locally. Use its JWT for /counter/me, /counter/settings,
# /counter/registers, /counter/shifts, /counter/stock/reconcile and /counter/audit.
# Create registers/providers/staff through documented owner routes as needed.
# Keep returned register device tokens private. Existing groups may explicitly
# deny permissions; operational roles never bypass those denials.
